# Restart MFD Portfolio Intelligence Server

## 1. SSH into Termux
```
ssh U0_a313@100.94.7.23 -p 8022
```

## 2. Enter proot Debian
```
proot-distro login debian --bind /storage/emulated/0:/root/storage
```

## 3. Start code-server (if not already running)
```
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
nohup code-server --bind-addr 0.0.0.0:8080 /root/storage/pictures/USB/MFD-Portfolio-Intelligence > ~/code-server.log 2>&1 &
disown
```
Access at: `http://100.94.7.23:8080`
Password: `cat ~/.config/code-server/config.yaml`

## 4. In code-server terminal — activate venv
```
source ~/venvs/mfd/bin/activate
```

## 5. Go to project and run Streamlit
```
cd /mnt/sdcard/pictures/USB/MFD-Portfolio-Intelligence
streamlit run app.py --server.port 8501 --server.address 0.0.0.0
```
Access at: `http://100.94.7.23:8501`

To run in background instead:
```
nohup streamlit run app.py --server.port 8501 --server.address 0.0.0.0 > ~/streamlit.log 2>&1 &
disown
```

## Notes
- Use `/mnt/sdcard/...` path, not `/root/storage/...` — the bind-mount path throws PermissionError on file writes (FUSE/exFAT write restriction). `/mnt/sdcard` works fine.
- If port 8501 busy: `pkill -f streamlit` or use a different port (`--server.port 8502`).
- venv location: `~/venvs/mfd` (proot's own ext4, not the FUSE-mounted USB drive — avoids symlink/write issues).